Warning: The stunts in this movie were performed by professionals, so neither you or
your dumb little buddies should attempt anything from this movie.

2
00:07:43,636 --> 00:07:49,636
Jackass 3.5 is a comedy, documentary, action film directed by Jeff Tremaine.

3
00:11:35,454 --> 00:11:41,454
Johnny Knoxville of 'Jackass' releases unused material of stunts, tricks, antics and shenanigans shot during the
production of 'Jackass 3D' that didn't make it into the film, as well as the hilarious outtakes.

4
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
Self, played by Johnny Knoxville.

5
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:25,090
Self, played by Ryan Dunn.

6
00:23:10,909 --> 00:23:16,909
Self, played by Dave England.

7
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:08,727
Self, played by Preston Lacy.

8
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
Self, played by Bam Margera.

9
00:34:46,363 --> 00:34:52,363
Self, played by Ehren McGhehey.

10
00:38:38,181 --> 00:38:44,181
Jackass 3D (known as Jackass 3 on home media) is a 2010 American
3D reality comedy film directed by Jeff Tremaine.

11
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
It is the third installment in the Jackass film series, and
the sequel to Jackass Number Two (2006).

12
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
The film stars the regular Jackass cast of  Johnny Knoxville, Bam Margera, Ryan Dunn, Steve-O,
"Danger Ehren" McGhehey, Dave England, Preston Lacy, Wee Man, and Chris Pontius.

13
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
This is the last Jackass film to feature Dunn before his death in 2011 and Margera as a primary
cast member before his departure in 2020 (Margera is briefly in Jackass Forever).

14
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
It is also the last Jackass film to feature a guest
appearance by Rip Taylor, who died in October 2019.

15
00:57:57,272 --> 00:58:03,272
The film was theatrically released in the United States in the 3D format on October 15, 2010, by
Paramount Pictures, marking the tenth anniversary of the Jackass television series.

16
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
It received generally positive reviews from critics.

17
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:46,909
The film grossed $171.7 million worldwide against a
production budget of $20 million.

18
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
A sequel, titled Jackass Forever, was released 12 years
later on February 4, 2022, to positive reviews.

19
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
Leftover film footage scenes was incorporated as an extended length feature
released as Jackass 3.5, on DVD and Blu-ray on June 14, 2011.

20
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film explores themes of snake, electric shock, buffalo, stunt, bungee-jump.

21
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
